# A guest node: the VMM (arg 2: a pool node on four vCPUs; it ran on one
# from 2026-09-18 to 2026-10-09 while a four-vCPU guest could start a
# thread on a null stack — a weak-memory race in the kernel's thread
# start record, fixed) boots a moss kernel in a virtual machine
# with the machine's second NIC and second entropy device passed through,
# and the guest joins this machine's fabric as node 2 — one box, two pool
# nodes. Lazy (no profiles): the Nodes app starts it through the machine's
# init (`machine-launch vmnode`) and stops it (`machine-unit-stop`), which
# destroys the VMM and with it the VM. Its budget is the guest's RAM
# (128 MB) plus the VMM's own; it nests in init's, so init's slice is
# sized for one guest beside a desktop. The hypervisor grant is honoured
# only by the system init and only when root holds the cap.
{
  image:  vmm
  arg:    2
  budget: { kobj: 8mb, user: 160mb }
  grant:  [log, bootfs, hypervisor]
  give: [
    { tag: device, device: rng, index: 1 }
    { tag: device, device: net, index: 1 }
  ]
}
